From: Dana Whitfield <dana.whitfield@hangs-gc.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS Construction Services 2026 Forms 1099
Date: Tue, 12 Jan 2027 11:05:00 -0800
Message-ID: <HGC-2026-1099@hangs-gc.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HGC_2026_1099_request"

--=_HGC_2026_1099_request
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

Attached are the 2026 vendor payments by vendor, the vendor master with each =
vendor's W-9 status and the accounts payable ledger by account. Please prepar=
e the 2026 Forms 1099-NEC and the transmittal summary for us to review; we fi=
le electronically.

The payments file is the final year-end export from accounts payable. A few t=
hings to look at:

- Ridgeline Concrete Cutting never sent a W-9. We started backup withholding =
in April after the third request.
- TIN Matching came back with no match for Cedar Hollow Tile in October. We a=
sked for a new W-9 and have not heard back.
- Tomas Arvelo is still on our list from the Q3 941 review; we have not decid=
ed whether he should have been on payroll.
- The September settlement went to the claimant's attorney, and our office re=
nt is paid to the landlord's LLC. I assume those are 1099-MISC, not NEC.

Thanks,
Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HGC_2026_1099_request
